speechtext:
Mr. Chairman, at five o'clock we had just passed subparagraph (xi) and it was my intention to move that a new subparagraph be added to be known as subparagraph (xii). I feel this is the proper
5.	1962	2541
Corporations and Labour Unions place to move that amendment which I will now have distributed.
I move:
That paragraph (a) of clause 4 be amended byadding thereto the following as subparagraph
(xii):
(xii) The name and address of each corporation or person with which the reporting corporation has an agreement or arrangement relating to one or more of the following:
(a)	The exchange of statistics;
(b)	The defining of product standards;
(c)	The exchange of credit information;
(d)	Definition of trade terms;
(e)	Co-operation in research and development;
(f)	Restriction of advertising;
(g)	Prices;
(h)	Quantity or quality of production;
(i)	Markets or customers; or
(j)	Channels or methods of distribution.
Perhaps I should explain to the committee what these are. All are contained in section 32 of the Combines Investigation Act. Briefly put, that section of the act generally prohibits agreements among companies for the purpose of fixing prices, limiting quantity or quality of production and engaging in restraint of trade practices. Another portion of section 32 of the Combines Investigation Act-
